diff --git a/src/gnd/examples/seeded_growth/seed.orm.yaml b/src/gnd/examples/seeded_growth/seed.orm.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d4e5e427
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/gnd/examples/seeded_growth/seed.orm.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# The owner-reviewed starting vocabulary (issue 222's seed): version 4, one
+# explicit, confirmed, alethic constraint with its review record.
+version: 4
+model_id: urn:example:seed@1
+source: {kind: text-conversation, mode: one-shot}
+object_types:
+  - {id: work, kind: value, name: WorkKey, primitive: String}
+  - {id: version, kind: value, name: VersionId, primitive: String}
+fact_types:
+  - id: work_has_version
+    reading: "{WorkKey} has version {VersionId}"
+    roles:
+      - {object_type: work, role_name: work}
+      - {object_type: version, role_name: version}
+    constraints:
+      - id: u1
+        type: uniqueness
+        roles: [version]
+        source: explicit
+        status: confirmed
+        modality: alethic
+        rationale: Each version belongs to one work.
+        provenance: {user_quote: "Each version belongs to one work.", reviewed_in: review-1}
diff --git a/src/gnd/skills/gnd-model-from-text/references/unattended-growth.md b/src/gnd/skills/gnd-model-from-text/references/unattended-growth.md
index c32e1738..9864e0b8 100644
--- a/src/gnd/skills/gnd-model-from-text/references/unattended-growth.md
+++ b/src/gnd/skills/gnd-model-from-text/references/unattended-growth.md
@@ -87,6 +87,30 @@ admits constraints it should have refused. The policy protects the facts it can
 those. The cells are in the
 [evolution contract](../../gnd-model-evolve/references/evolution-contract.md#additive-policy).
 
+## Starting from a reviewed vocabulary
+
+A growth run can start from a vocabulary an owner has already reviewed, without restating its claims
+as unreviewed. Put the reviewed model in its own file (version 1 to 4, not unattended) and make the
+growth root a version-5 model with `source.mode: unattended` and `reviewer: none` that includes it by
+id, path and SHA-256. The root needs no document of its own while it holds nothing but the include;
+the first round declares one with a `source-document` add.
+
+What the rules ask of each side is stated once, in
+[Unattended source](../../gnd-orm-core/references/representation-format.md#an-unattended-root-that-includes-a-reviewed-model):
+the included elements keep their own source, status and modality; everything a round adds is the
+root's and keeps every rule. A round may add object types, fact types and constraints, and may attach
+constraints to an included fact type (`fact_type_constraints`); it cannot change, rename or delete an
+included element, and it cannot re-pin an include. `gnd validate` prints one `INCLUDE` line per
+include, naming what it carries. The new constraint's source follows
+[Evolve admission (D-12)](../../gnd-orm-core/references/provenance-and-modality.md#evolve-admission-d-12).
+
+The packaged example `src/gnd/examples/seeded_growth/` runs the whole path: a seed, an empty root,
+two rounds, then `gnd validate`, `gnd check` and `gnd judgments check`.
+
+When the vocabulary cannot be included (it is unattended itself, or nests includes), carry its claims
+into the root as `imported`, `proposed` and `deontic`, with the vocabulary file as the root's first
+document and a span on each element. Inside the growth model those claims then read as unreviewed.
+
 ## Evidence for Steps 3 to 7
 
 For each step: the text that licenses a proposal, what to propose, and what does not license
diff --git a/src/gnd/skills/gnd-orm-core/references/representation-format.md b/src/gnd/skills/gnd-orm-core/references/representation-format.md
index e575d2c3..0a1218e9 100644
--- a/src/gnd/skills/gnd-orm-core/references/representation-format.md
+++ b/src/gnd/skills/gnd-orm-core/references/representation-format.md
@@ -1963,6 +1963,8 @@ above):
 | `gnd flatten` | writes the flat model and its flattening record (below) for any include root, temporal or not |
 | `gnd export pyrel` (default, `--rules duckdb`, `--rules lqp`) | exports the flat model and records the flattening record's SHA-256 and each pin ([PyRel page](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/blob/main/docs/runtimes/pyrel.md)); the default mode still refuses temporal models |
 | `gnd judgments check` | receipts bind the root file's sha256 (`subject.model_sha256`), which commits to every include's pin; references bind under `--reference-root` as for any model. An include refusal reports `reason: "binding"` with the include code as `message` |
+| `gnd coverage` | the composed model |
+| `gnd evolve` (preview, apply, finalize) | the authored root as the candidate; included elements are read-only and owned constraints attach to included fact types (the gnd-model-evolve evolution contract, "Shared vocabulary evolution") |
 
 An include path that cannot be encoded as UTF-8 is refused `include:path`
 with the other path checks, on every route.
