reference_populations:
  - id: catalog
    path: references/catalog.pop.json
    sha256: <64 lowercase hexadecimal digits of the exact file bytes>
    fact_types: [catalog_pair]
```

Each declaration has exactly these four fields. IDs are unique, nonempty and at
most 128 characters. Ownership is disjoint across declarations and covers only
existing base fact types. Candidate populations cannot mention owned fact types,
even with an empty list. Operations may read them but cannot assert or retract
them. References use ordinary population formats 1/2 and assert only their owned
fact types; they cannot include further references.

Paths are confined POSIX relative paths beneath the explicit model parent, with
no symlink in the root, ancestors or leaf. At most 32 files, 32 MiB in total,
10 MiB per input, 32 path components and 4096 path characters are admitted.
The combined view admits at most 100000 asserted rows and 100000 instance entries,
counted separately; reference container depth is at most 64. Reached attempted
combined join work is capped at 100000 before materialization and deduplication.
Input refusal is band 3; exceeded evaluation work is unchecked, band 4 unless
an independent definite violation establishes band 1.

Model and reference bytes bind once per invocation. A loaded model retains its
context; `load_model_bytes` requires `bind_references(model, root=...)` and an
explicit matching `references=` context at use. The combined view supplies fixed
facts to constraints and derivations. Candidate counts and admission contain
only candidate occurrences. Reference-bearing reports use the closed version-12
wrapper with a binding roster and asserted occurrence origins; embedded reports
retain their existing mechanical version. Reference identity binds normalized
model content plus sorted declarations, including path, ownership and expected
raw hash. `model_id` remains a separate opaque identifier. Versions 1–3 reject
this field; a feature-free version 4 retains the ordinary wire and behavior.

Check, composition, witness, batch, transition and diff consume bound references. Synth, codegen and
older session contracts refuse reference-bearing inputs before publishing
artifacts or invoking an adapter. Conformance can report changed model identity;
it never regenerates code. Extraction projects candidate-owned fact types only.

## Repair annotations

Every constraint may carry `owner: candidate | reference | host` and an optional
unique `allowed_fixes` list drawn from `add-fact`, `replace-fact`, `delete-fact`
and `replace-artifact` (at most four). Missing owner means candidate. These
annotations describe repair responsibility; they do not change evaluation,
modality, provenance, coverage floors or acceptance. Verbalization preserves
them as metadata and does not invent a rule. Session behavior lives in
[the v7 contract](../../gnd-dev-session/references/session-v7-contract.md).

For explicitly selected saved opinion evidence, see the [judgment contract](../../gnd-dev-session/references/judgment-contract.md).


## Model includes (version 5)

A project model can include a tool's shared vocabulary without copying its
object types, fact types or constraints. This section is the normative home
for version-5 model composition; workflow notes and how-to pages cite it.

```yaml
version: 5
includes:
  - id: components
    path: vocab/components-v1.orm.yaml
    sha256: <64 lowercase hexadecimal digits of the exact file bytes>
fact_type_constraints:
  - fact_type: component_imports_component
    constraints:
      - id: no_import_loops
        type: ring
        variant: acyclic
        source: user-supplied
        status: confirmed
        modality: alethic
        provenance: {user_quote: "No component may import itself, directly or indirectly."}
```

`includes` is a nonempty list of at most eight entries. Each entry has exactly
`id`, `path` and `sha256`. Its id is a unique string of 1–128 characters;
its digest is 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters. Include-bearing models
use version 5 and may omit `object_types` and `fact_types`. An include-free
version-5 model has version-4 semantics and identities that also cover its
version. Earlier model versions remain admitted under their existing rules.

Each path is confined POSIX relative to the explicit model parent/root:
at most 32 nonempty components and 4,096 characters, no absolute path,
dot/parent component, backslash, NUL or drive prefix. Neither the root nor
any included path ancestor or leaf may be a symlink. Each included file
is a regular file read with a 10 MiB cap; the entire included set is at
most 32 MiB. Hashes cover raw bytes, including whitespace and final newlines.

An included file is a standalone-valid model at version 1–4, declaring its
object types and fact types and optionally constraints and deontic notes.
It cannot declare `includes`, `reference_populations`, `operations`,
`rejected_proposals` or `fact_type_constraints`, even as empty lists. Its
source mode cannot be `unattended`; an unattended root may include it, and
[Unattended source](#unattended-source) says what its rules ask of the
included elements. Nesting is not admitted. The includer's
version, model id and source govern composition; each included file's
version, model id and source are retained privately as origin metadata.

Composition retains the includer's own elements first, in authored order,
then appends each include's object types, fact types, constraints and notes
in declaration order. All ids of object types, fact types, operations and
active named constraints share one namespace: a duplicate refuses, never
overrides. Anonymous constraints are tracked by structural address.

`fact_type_constraints` is available only with includes. It is a nonempty
list of mappings with exactly `fact_type` and `constraints`; the target is
a nonempty fact-type id and constraints is a nonempty list of ordinary
inline constraints. The target must originate in an include. These owned
constraints append after the target's included inline constraints. They
remain project-owned; they are not vocabulary overrides. Existing top-level
constraint kinds remain top-level. Own operations, derivations, subtypes
and reference declarations resolve against the full composition.

Resolution runs in this order, each stage across all includes before the next:

1. Parse the including bytes with the existing suffix-sensitive parser.
2. Validate declarations, then the includer's structural schema.
3. Validate every confined path.
4. Read every included file, enforcing per-file and set caps.
5. Verify every raw digest; never parse mismatched bytes.
6. Parse every included file with its declared suffix (`.json` is strict JSON).
7. Refuse forbidden sections and unattended included sources.
8. Validate every included document standalone.
9. Merge, resolve attachment targets, then check the shared id namespace.
10. Validate composed structure and semantics, remap issues/warnings, construct
    the model, validate reference declarations and compile obligations.
11. Bind reference populations under the same retained root.

Include refusals are `ModelValidationError` issues in input band 3. Reasons:
`include:declaration`, `include:path`, `include:unreadable`, `include:size`,
`include:hash-mismatch`, `include:parse`, `include:forbidden-section`,
`include:invalid-included-model`, `include:unknown-target`, `include:collision`.
A document whose nested containers cannot be safely copied refuses
`include:declaration`; direct composer callers receive the same issue band.
They identify declarations or structural addresses without population values.
Diagnostics inside included elements use `includes[ID]:<original address>`.
The deepest origin wins: an owned inline attachment on an included host
reports its authored `$.fact_type_constraints[i].constraints[j]` address.
Warnings use the same origin mapping; ValidationIssue gains no new field.

`load_model(path)` resolves includes. The explicit rooted bytes entry point
is `load_model_bytes_composed(data, *, source, root)`. Unrooted
`load_model_bytes` refuses any `includes` key with `include:unresolved`,
even if malformed; orphan `fact_type_constraints` refuses
`include:declaration`. Unsupported consumers refuse declared includes or
attachments with `include:unsupported-route` before loading, copying,
performing model-identity/currency work or publishing a partial model.
The bounded reader may still produce its internal intake snapshot hash. A
refused closed-format batch report computes its authentic captured-byte
digest only as refusal metadata after detection; it never evaluates or
claims currency for that composition. Portable standalone skill scripts
have their own nonzero refusal and direct callers to `gnd validate`.

CLI routes that resolve an include root (every other route refuses it as
above):

| Route | What it binds |
|---|---|
| `gnd validate`, `gnd check` | the composed model; `model_digest` is its composed identity |
| `gnd extract` (non-temporal models), `gnd verify` | the root's sha256 and each pin, through the extraction flattening record below |
| `gnd compose` | the composed model, with stale pins refused before population input |
| `gnd flatten` | writes the flat model and its flattening record (below) for any include root, temporal or not |
| `gnd export pyrel` (default, `--rules duckdb`, `--rules lqp`) | exports the flat model and records the flattening record's SHA-256 and each pin ([PyRel page](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/blob/main/docs/runtimes/pyrel.md)); the default mode still refuses temporal models |
| `gnd judgments check` | receipts bind the root file's sha256 (`subject.model_sha256`), which commits to every include's pin; references bind under `--reference-root` as for any model. An include refusal reports `reason: "binding"` with the include code as `message` |
| `gnd coverage` | the composed model |
| `gnd evolve` (preview, apply, finalize) | the authored root as the candidate; included elements are read-only and owned constraints attach to included fact types (the gnd-model-evolve evolution contract, "Shared vocabulary evolution") |

An include path that cannot be encoded as UTF-8 is refused `include:path`
with the other path checks, on every route.

`load_model_bytes_composed(..., bind_references=False)` composes and
authenticates the includes without binding references, for a caller that
binds them under another root.

Existing identity functions cover the loaded composition and its authored
include/attachment declarations, with their existing field exclusions.
Include paths therefore participate in identity. The model dump and identity
functions exclude private origin metadata. Empty include/attachment fields are omitted from
both model dump entry points, preserving include-free serializations.
A raw includer hash commits to the pinned bytes but cannot prove their
presence or validity: any positive freshness/publication claim additionally
requires verification of the included bytes in that same invocation.

### Extraction flattening record

Path-based `gnd extract` supports a resolved include-bearing root when the
effective model is eligible for extraction. It publishes
`<stem>.flat.orm.json` and `<stem>.flattening.json` alongside the ordinary
bundle. The artifact index binds both file digests and names them in a
`flattening` object with keys `flat_model` and `record`. The `model.sha256`
field still identifies the authored root. Include-free bundles omit the
two files and the `flattening` object. Bundle publication refuses output
destinations that overlap the bound root, include or reference files.

The flat model is canonical JSON accepted by unrooted model-byte intake.
Resolved elements keep their order and identities, with project-owned
attachments materialized as inline constraints. The wire omits the consumed
include and attachment declarations, load-time warnings, and the usual
empty or null re-entry defaults. Reference declarations retain their
authored-root coordinate for later path-based binding. Each published
flattening artifact has a 10 MiB limit.

`gnd flatten MODEL --out DIR` writes the same two files for any include
root, temporal or not, without the bundle or its index: both files or
"""MG5 unattended source mode (model-growth-guardrails milestone).

A separate home inside the ``gnd.model`` package so ``_validation`` stays under
its RF6 size ceiling. ``_rule_unattended`` is registered last in
``gnd.model._validation._SEMANTIC_RULES`` and ``unattended_span_issues`` is
re-exported by ``gnd.model``. ``_validation`` registers its constraint and
provenance walks here at import time, so this module never imports
``_validation`` back.

One rule family, one walk (MG-R2). Gated on ``source.mode: unattended``, so no
model without the mode gains or loses an issue (MG-R1). The rule table is
normative in gnd-orm-core/references/representation-format.md ("Unattended
source").
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import hashlib
import re
from collections.abc import Callable, Iterator, Mapping
from contextvars import ContextVar
from dataclasses import dataclass
from typing import Any, Literal

from gnd.errors import ValidationIssue

#: The shared walks and the element label, registered by
#: ``gnd.model._validation`` once they are defined. This home never imports
#: ``_validation``: even a per-call import is a runtime edge, and the two
#: would form the cycle the RF8 graph check forbids.
_constraint_walk: Callable[[dict[str, Any]], Iterator[tuple[str, dict[str, Any]]]] | None = None
_provenance_walk: Callable[[dict[str, Any]], Iterator[tuple[str, dict[str, Any]]]] | None = None
_provenance_label: Callable[[dict[str, Any]], str] | None = None


def _iter_constraints(doc: dict[str, Any]):
    if _constraint_walk is None:
        raise RuntimeError("gnd.model._validation has not registered the constraint walk")
    return _constraint_walk(doc)


def _iter_provenance_bearing(doc: dict[str, Any]):
    if _provenance_walk is None:
        raise RuntimeError("gnd.model._validation has not registered the provenance walk")
    return _provenance_walk(doc)


def _provenance_bearing_label(element: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    if _provenance_label is None:
        raise RuntimeError("gnd.model._validation has not registered the provenance label")
    return _provenance_label(element)


UNATTENDED_MODE = "unattended"
_SHA256_HEX = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{64}")  # always fullmatch: `$` admits a trailing newline (review R-F1)
_SPAN_KEYS = frozenset({"document_sha256", "start", "end", "excerpt_sha256"})
_UNATTENDED_SPANLESS_SOURCE = "common-sense"
_UNATTENDED_INDUCED_SOURCE = "induced"
_UNATTENDED_ALETHIC_SOURCES = ("sample", "llm-inferred", "common-sense", "induced")

#: VG3: ``id()`` of the composed document's elements whose origin is an
#: include, set by ``gnd.model._model_warnings`` around ``semantic_validate``
#: and by nothing else (``gnd.model._includes.included_rows`` computes it).
#: Every other caller sees the empty set, and so today's rules.
_INCLUDED: ContextVar[frozenset[int]] = ContextVar("gnd_unattended_included", default=frozenset())


def _declared_spans(owner: Any, declared: set[str], *, samples: bool) -> Iterator[tuple[str, Any]]:
    """(suffix, span) for each span an included element carries over a document the root declares.

    D14 (a): such a span is the root's business and keeps U7's shape check;
    any other span an included element carries is read by no rule.
    """
    provenance = owner.get("provenance") if isinstance(owner, Mapping) else None
    if not isinstance(provenance, Mapping):
        return
    for index, span in enumerate(_listed(provenance.get("spans"))):
        if isinstance(span, Mapping) and isinstance(span.get("document_sha256"), str) \
                and span["document_sha256"] in declared:
            yield f".provenance.spans[{index}]", span
    # Sample spans belong to fact types, the one place the span walk visits them
    # (VG3 review r1, F1).
    for index, entry in enumerate(_listed(provenance.get("sample_spans")) if samples else []):
        span = entry.get("span") if isinstance(entry, Mapping) else None
        if isinstance(span, Mapping) and isinstance(span.get("document_sha256"), str) \
                and span["document_sha256"] in declared:
            yield f".provenance.sample_spans[{index}].span", span


def _unattended_source(doc: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    source = doc.get("source")
    if isinstance(source, Mapping) and source.get("mode") == UNATTENDED_MODE:
        return dict(source)
    return None


def _listed(value: Any) -> list[Any]:
    """A collection the rule may walk: a list, else nothing (review R-F14)."""
    return value if isinstance(value, list) else []


def _is_int(value: Any) -> bool:
    return isinstance(value, int) and not isinstance(value, bool)


def _declared_documents(source: dict[str, Any], issues: list[ValidationIssue], *, rule_id: str,
                        first_document_pending: bool = False) -> set[str]:
    def issue(path: str, message: str) -> None:
        issues.append(ValidationIssue(path=path, message=message, rule_id=rule_id))

    if source.get("reviewer") != "none":
        issue("$.source.reviewer", "an unattended model must declare reviewer: none")
    documents = source.get("documents")
    declared: set[str] = set()
    if not isinstance(documents, list) or not documents:
        # VG4 (D4 (a)): a root that includes a reviewed model and holds nothing of
        # its own may wait for its first document; a growth round declares it.
        # Absent or empty only: a present null cannot take the first round's add
        # (VG4 review r1, F1).
        if not (first_document_pending and ("documents" not in source or documents == [])):
            issue("$.source.documents", "an unattended model must declare at least one source document")
        return declared
    for index, entry in enumerate(documents):
        if (
            isinstance(entry, Mapping)
            and set(entry) == {"sha256", "label"}
            and isinstance(entry.get("sha256"), str)
            and _SHA256_HEX.fullmatch(entry["sha256"])
            and isinstance(entry.get("label"), str)
            and entry["label"].strip()
        ):
            declared.add(entry["sha256"])
        else:
            issue(f"$.source.documents[{index}]",
                  "a source document is {sha256: 64 lowercase hex, label: non-empty string}, nothing else")
    return declared


def _span_issue(span: Any, path: str, declared: set[str], *, rule_id: str) -> ValidationIssue | None:
    if not isinstance(span, Mapping) or set(span) != _SPAN_KEYS:
        reason = "a span is {document_sha256, start, end, excerpt_sha256}, nothing else"
    elif not all(isinstance(span[key], str) and _SHA256_HEX.fullmatch(span[key])
                 for key in ("document_sha256", "excerpt_sha256")):
        reason = "span digests are 64 lowercase hex"
    elif not (_is_int(span["start"]) and _is_int(span["end"])):
        reason = "span offsets are integers"
    elif not 0 <= span["start"] < span["end"]:
        reason = "a span needs 0 <= start < end"
    elif span["document_sha256"] not in declared:
        reason = "the span names a document the source does not declare"
    else:
        return None
    return ValidationIssue(path=path, message=reason, rule_id=rule_id)


def _require_spans(owner: Any, path: str, label: str, declared: set[str], issues: list[ValidationIssue], *,
                   rule_id: str, span_rule_id: str) -> None:
    provenance = owner.get("provenance") if isinstance(owner, Mapping) else None
    spans = provenance.get("spans") if isinstance(provenance, Mapping) else None
    if not isinstance(spans, list) or not spans:
        issues.append(ValidationIssue(path=path, message=f"{label} cites no source span (provenance.spans)",
                                      rule_id=rule_id))
        return
    for index, span in enumerate(spans):
        found = _span_issue(span, f"{path}.provenance.spans[{index}]", declared, rule_id=span_rule_id)
        if found is not None:
            issues.append(found)


def _sample_span_issues(fact_type: dict[str, Any], path: str, declared: set[str], issues: list[ValidationIssue], *,
                        rule_id: str, span_rule_id: str) -> None:
    rows = fact_type.get("sample_population")
    count = len(rows) if isinstance(rows, list) else 0
    provenance = fact_type.get("provenance")
    entries = provenance.get("sample_spans") if isinstance(provenance, Mapping) else None
    target = f"{path}.provenance.sample_spans"
    if not count and entries is None:
        return
    if not isinstance(entries, list):
        issues.append(ValidationIssue(path=target, message="sample rows cite no source spans (provenance.sample_spans)",
                                      rule_id=rule_id))
        return
    covered: set[int] = set()
    for index, entry in enumerate(entries):
        row = entry.get("row") if isinstance(entry, Mapping) else None
        if not isinstance(entry, Mapping) or set(entry) != {"row", "span"} or not _is_int(row):
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(path=f"{target}[{index}]", message="a sample span is {row: integer, span}",
                                          rule_id=rule_id))
            continue
        if row in covered or not 0 <= row < count:
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(
                path=f"{target}[{index}].row", message=f"sample span row {row} is repeated or names no sample row",
                rule_id=rule_id))
        covered.add(row)
        found = _span_issue(entry.get("span"), f"{target}[{index}].span", declared, rule_id=span_rule_id)
        if found is not None:
            issues.append(found)
    missing = sorted(set(range(count)) - covered)
    if missing:
        issues.append(ValidationIssue(
            path=target, message=f"sample rows {missing} cite no source span", rule_id=rule_id))


def _rule_unattended(doc: dict[str, Any]) -> list[ValidationIssue]:
    """MG5: the unattended source mode, U1..U8, one walk; nothing without the mode."""
    source = _unattended_source(doc)
    raw = doc.get("source")
    mode = raw.get("mode") if isinstance(raw, Mapping) else None
    if source is None:
        # Close review R3-1: a near-miss spelling would silently switch the
        # family off; say so (a warning: the mode is not declared).
        near_miss = [
            ValidationIssue(path="$.source.mode", rule_id="semantic:unattended-u1", severity="warning",
                            message=f"source.mode {mode!r} is not 'unattended'; the unattended rules do not apply")
        ] if isinstance(mode, str) and mode.strip().casefold() == UNATTENDED_MODE else []
        # The schema admits `spans` on the otherwise closed induced provenance
        # only for this mode; outside it the key stays refused, as before MG5
        # (close review R4-F1: no MG-R1 exception).
        return near_miss + [
            ValidationIssue(path=f"{path}.provenance.spans", rule_id="semantic:unattended-u7",
                            message="provenance.spans on an induced constraint requires source.mode: unattended")
            for path, constraint in _iter_constraints(doc)
            if constraint.get("source") == "induced" and isinstance(constraint.get("provenance"), Mapping)
            and "spans" in constraint["provenance"]
        ]
    issues: list[ValidationIssue] = []
    included = _INCLUDED.get()
    declared = _declared_documents(source, issues, rule_id="semantic:unattended-u1",
                                   first_document_pending=_owns_nothing(doc, included))
    for path, element in _iter_provenance_bearing(doc):
        if id(element) in included:
            continue  # VG3: an included element's status is the include's (U2)
        if element.get("status") == "confirmed":
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(
                path=path, message=f"{_provenance_bearing_label(element)} is confirmed, but no reviewer exists",
                rule_id="semantic:unattended-u2"))
    constraints = list(_iter_constraints(doc))
    for path, constraint in constraints:
        if id(constraint) in included:
            continue  # VG3 (U3)
        if constraint.get("source") in ("explicit", "user-supplied"):
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(
                path=path, message=f"source '{constraint.get('source')}' claims a human said it; nobody did",
                rule_id="semantic:unattended-u3"))
    for collection, label in (("object_types", "object type"), ("fact_types", "fact type")):
        for element in _listed(doc.get(collection)):
            if isinstance(element, Mapping) and id(element) in included:
                _included_span_issues(element, f"$.{collection}[id={element.get('id', '?')}]", declared, issues,
                                      samples=collection == "fact_types")
            elif isinstance(element, Mapping):
                _require_spans(element, f"$.{collection}[id={element.get('id', '?')}]", label, declared, issues,
                               rule_id="semantic:unattended-u4", span_rule_id="semantic:unattended-u7")
    for path, constraint in constraints:
        if id(constraint) in included:
            _included_span_issues(constraint, path, declared, issues, samples=False)  # VG3: U5 asks nothing
            continue
        provenance = constraint.get("provenance")
        has_spans = isinstance(provenance, Mapping) and "spans" in provenance
        # An induced constraint cites the digest-bound population evidence in
        # its induction block in place of a span (issue #148).
        cites_population = constraint.get("source") == _UNATTENDED_INDUCED_SOURCE and isinstance(
            provenance, Mapping) and isinstance(provenance.get("induction"), Mapping)
        spanless = not has_spans and (
            constraint.get("source") == _UNATTENDED_SPANLESS_SOURCE or cites_population)
        if not spanless:
            # A common-sense or induced constraint needs no span, but a span it
            # does carry is checked like any other (review R-F6).
            _require_spans(constraint, path, "constraint", declared, issues,
                           rule_id="semantic:unattended-u5", span_rule_id="semantic:unattended-u7")
    for fact_type in _listed(doc.get("fact_types")):
        if isinstance(fact_type, Mapping) and id(fact_type) not in included:  # VG3: U6; U7 above
            _sample_span_issues(dict(fact_type), f"$.fact_types[id={fact_type.get('id', '?')}]", declared, issues,
                                rule_id="semantic:unattended-u6", span_rule_id="semantic:unattended-u7")
    # Every provenance-bearing element, obligations and operations included:
    # D-03 is an error in this mode (close review R3-2).
    for path, element in _iter_provenance_bearing(doc):
        if id(element) in included and element.get("status") == "confirmed":
            continue  # VG3, D13 (a): an included element is exempt from U8 only when confirmed
        if element.get("modality") == "alethic" and element.get("source") in _UNATTENDED_ALETHIC_SOURCES:
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(
                path=path,
                message=f"an unreviewed {element.get('source')} {_provenance_bearing_label(element)} cannot be alethic in unattended mode",
                rule_id="semantic:unattended-u8"))
    order = {f"semantic:unattended-u{n}": n for n in range(1, 9)}
    return sorted(issues, key=lambda issue: order[issue.rule_id])


#: The sections composition appends included entries to (``_includes.SECTIONS``).
_MERGED_SECTIONS = ("object_types", "fact_types", "constraints", "deontic_notes")
_HEADER_KEYS = frozenset({"version", "model_id", "source", "includes"})


def _owns_nothing(doc: dict[str, Any], included: frozenset[int]) -> bool:
    """VG4 (D4 (a)): the root declares includes and nothing of its own.

    Read on the composed document with VG3's origin set, which is the root's
    own document as authored: composition appends only included entries to the
    four merged sections, an attachment enters an included fact type as the
    root's, and an include cannot declare any other section.
    """
    if not _listed(doc.get("includes")):
        return False
    for key, value in doc.items():
        if key in _HEADER_KEYS:
            continue
        if key in _MERGED_SECTIONS:
            if value is not None and not isinstance(value, list):
                return False
            for element in _listed(value):
                if id(element) not in included:
                    return False
                if key == "fact_types" and isinstance(element, Mapping) and any(
                        id(constraint) not in included for constraint in _listed(element.get("constraints"))):
                    return False
        elif value is not None and value != [] and value != {}:
            return False
    return True


def _included_span_issues(owner: Any, path: str, declared: set[str], issues: list[ValidationIssue], *,
                          samples: bool) -> None:
    """U7 over the spans an included element carries over a root-declared document (D14 (a))."""
    for suffix, span in _declared_spans(owner, declared, samples=samples):
        found = _span_issue(span, f"{path}{suffix}", declared, rule_id="semantic:unattended-u7")
        if found is not None:
            issues.append(found)


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class SpanCoverage:
    """UG3: how many of an unattended model's source spans one ``--document`` run re-hashed.

    A span counts as re-hashed when its document was supplied, decoded, and
    its shape is valid (whether it then matched, mismatched or ran out of
    range). Everything else counts as unchecked, failing closed. The counting
    table is normative in representation-format.md ("Unattended source")."""

    total: int
    rehashed: int

    @property
    def unchecked(self) -> int:
        return self.total - self.rehashed

    def issue(self, *, severity: Literal["error", "warning"]) -> ValidationIssue | None:
        """The one ``unattended:spans-unchecked`` entry, or ``None`` when every span was re-hashed."""
        if not self.unchecked:
            return None
        return ValidationIssue(
            path="$.source.documents", rule_id="unattended:spans-unchecked", severity=severity,
            message=f"{self.unchecked} of {self.total} source spans were not re-hashed; "
                    "supply every declared document with --document")


def _span_walk(doc: dict[str, Any], documents: Mapping[str, bytes],
               included: frozenset[int] = frozenset()) -> tuple[list[ValidationIssue], SpanCoverage]:
    from gnd.anchors import AnchorError, canonical_document_text

    source = _unattended_source(doc) or {}
    declared = {entry.get("sha256") for entry in source.get("documents") or [] if isinstance(entry, Mapping)}
    supplied: dict[str, tuple[str, str]] = {}
    issues: list[ValidationIssue] = []
    for display, raw in documents.items():
        digest = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()
        if digest not in declared:
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(path=display, rule_id="unattended:document-undeclared",
                                          message=f"document sha256 {digest} is not declared in source.documents"))
            continue
        try:
            supplied[digest] = (display, canonical_document_text(raw))
        except AnchorError as error:
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(path=display, rule_id="unattended:document-unreadable",
                                          message=f"document is not strict UTF-8 text: {error}".replace(
                                              "anchor:sidecar-invalid: ", "")))
    total = rehashed = 0
    for path, span, from_include in _iter_unattended_spans(doc, included):
        if from_include and not (isinstance(span, Mapping) and isinstance(span.get("document_sha256"), str)
                                 and span["document_sha256"] in declared):
            continue  # VG3, D14 (a): an included span over another document is not the root's claim
        total += 1
        # Shape first: a digest that is not a string is never a key (UG3 review finding 4).
        digest = span.get("document_sha256") if isinstance(span, Mapping) else None
        if not isinstance(digest, str) or digest not in supplied:
            continue
        if _span_issue(span, path, set(supplied), rule_id="unattended:span-invalid") is not None:
            continue
        rehashed += 1
        _display, text = supplied[span["document_sha256"]]
        if span["end"] > len(text):
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(path=path, rule_id="unattended:span-out-of-range",
                                          message=f"span end {span['end']} is past the document's {len(text)} code points"))
        elif hashlib.sha256(text[span["start"]:span["end"]].encode("utf-8")).hexdigest() != span["excerpt_sha256"]:
            issues.append(ValidationIssue(path=path, rule_id="unattended:excerpt-mismatch",
                                          message=f"the excerpt at [{span['start']}, {span['end']}) has a different sha256"))
    return issues, SpanCoverage(total=total, rehashed=rehashed)


def unattended_span_issues(doc: dict[str, Any], documents: Mapping[str, bytes], *,
                           included: frozenset[int] = frozenset()) -> list[ValidationIssue]:
    """MG5 `gnd validate --document`: re-hash every valid span over a supplied document.

    ``documents`` maps a display path to raw bytes. Offsets count code points
    of the NFC text of the strict UTF-8 decoding (``canonical_document_text``);
    ``documents[].sha256`` is over the raw bytes. Messages name paths, digests
    and offsets, never document text (MG-R5). ``included`` is
    ``gnd.model.included_rows`` over ``doc`` (VG3)."""
    return _span_walk(doc, documents, included)[0]


def unattended_span_coverage(doc: dict[str, Any], documents: Mapping[str, bytes], *,
                             included: frozenset[int] = frozenset()) -> SpanCoverage | None:
    """UG3: the span counts of one ``--document`` run; ``None`` without the unattended mode."""
    if _unattended_source(doc) is None:
        return None
    return _span_walk(doc, documents, included)[1]


def _iter_unattended_spans(doc: dict[str, Any], included: frozenset[int] = frozenset()):
    """(path, span, whether its owner came from an include) for every span the walk visits."""
    def spans_of(owner: Any, path: str):
        provenance = owner.get("provenance") if isinstance(owner, Mapping) else None
        # Total over any shape (UG3 review finding 2): outside the mode, layer one
        # does not check `provenance.spans`, and `--document` still walks it.
        for index, span in enumerate(_listed(provenance.get("spans")) if isinstance(provenance, Mapping) else []):
            yield f"{path}.provenance.spans[{index}]", span, id(owner) in included

    for collection in ("object_types", "fact_types"):
        for element in _listed(doc.get(collection)):
            if isinstance(element, Mapping):
                yield from spans_of(element, f"$.{collection}[id={element.get('id', '?')}]")
    for path, constraint in _iter_constraints(doc):
        yield from spans_of(constraint, path)
    for fact_type in _listed(doc.get("fact_types")):
        provenance = fact_type.get("provenance") if isinstance(fact_type, Mapping) else None
        entries = provenance.get("sample_spans") if isinstance(provenance, Mapping) else None
        for index, entry in enumerate(entries if isinstance(entries, list) else []):
            if isinstance(entry, Mapping):
                yield (f"$.fact_types[id={fact_type.get('id', '?')}].provenance.sample_spans[{index}].span",
                       entry.get("span"), id(fact_type) in included)

