Warnings use the same origin mapping; ValidationIssue gains no new field.

`load_model(path)` resolves includes. The explicit rooted bytes entry point
is `load_model_bytes_composed(data, *, source, root)`. Unrooted
`load_model_bytes` refuses any `includes` key with `include:unresolved`,
even if malformed; orphan `fact_type_constraints` refuses
`include:declaration`. Unsupported consumers refuse declared includes or
attachments with `include:unsupported-route` before loading, copying,
performing model-identity/currency work or publishing a partial model.
The bounded reader may still produce its internal intake snapshot hash. A
refused closed-format batch report computes its authentic captured-byte
digest only as refusal metadata after detection; it never evaluates or
claims currency for that composition. Portable standalone skill scripts
have their own nonzero refusal and direct callers to `gnd validate`.

CLI routes that resolve an include root (every other route refuses it as
above):

| Route | What it binds |
|---|---|
| `gnd validate`, `gnd check` | the composed model; `model_digest` is its composed identity |
| `gnd extract` (non-temporal models), `gnd verify` | the root's sha256 and each pin, through the extraction flattening record below |
| `gnd compose` | the composed model, with stale pins refused before population input |
| `gnd flatten` | writes the flat model and its flattening record (below) for any include root, temporal or not |
| `gnd export pyrel` (default, `--rules duckdb`, `--rules lqp`) | exports the flat model and records the flattening record's SHA-256 and each pin ([PyRel page](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/blob/main/docs/runtimes/pyrel.md)); the default mode still refuses temporal models |
| `gnd judgments check` | receipts bind the root file's sha256 (`subject.model_sha256`), which commits to every include's pin; references bind under `--reference-root` as for any model. An include refusal reports `reason: "binding"` with the include code as `message` |
| `gnd coverage` | the composed model |
| `gnd evolve` (preview, apply, finalize) | the authored root as the candidate; included elements are read-only and owned constraints attach to included fact types (the gnd-model-evolve evolution contract, "Shared vocabulary evolution") |

An include path that cannot be encoded as UTF-8 is refused `include:path`
with the other path checks, on every route.

`load_model_bytes_composed(..., bind_references=False)` composes and
authenticates the includes without binding references, for a caller that
binds them under another root.

Existing identity functions cover the loaded composition and its authored
include/attachment declarations, with their existing field exclusions.
Include paths therefore participate in identity. The model dump and identity
functions exclude private origin metadata. Empty include/attachment fields are omitted from
both model dump entry points, preserving include-free serializations.
